WEBVTT

00:01:28.252 --> 00:01:31.200
"In Rainbows." Buyers could determine the price,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.050
but the offer was exclusive, and only stood for a limited period of time.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:40.009
The album sold more copies than previous releases of the band.

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:43.206
The Danish chocolate company Anthon Berg

00:01:43.206 --> 00:01:46.388
opened a so-called "generous store" in Copenhagen.

00:01:46.388 --> 00:01:48.807
It asked customers to purchase chocolate

00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:52.306
with the promise of good deeds towards loved ones.

00:01:52.306 --> 00:01:55.220
It turned transactions into interactions,

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:57.773
and generosity into a currency.

00:01:57.773 --> 00:02:00.734
Companies can even give control to hackers.